#### Finding 2: Types of plastic
**What I found:**  
There is not one single type of plastic. For the general public there are seven codes. Each plastic has a slightly different composition. 
For example code one is polythylene Trephthalane (PET). One of the common types of plastic you use in your house, or High-density Polythylene. (HDPE). This is what most of you're food containers are made out of.
Each type of plastic has its own way of being recycled. Not all can be recycled the same way, some require different chemicals.
**Why it matters to our project:**  
We can not focus on every type of plastic in one machine. Doing so will extreemly costly. We should focus on the most profitable type of plastic, and the most abundant, such as HDPE
Focusing on one type of plastic will save us money, and allow us to cater to a wider audience. 
**Source:**  
Plastic-material-specific-data: https://www.epa.gov/facts-and-figures-about-materials-waste-and-recycling/plastics-material-specific-data

#### Finding 3: The process of recycling and remanufacturing

**What I found:**  
Plasic is made out of chemicals. Some chemicals are worth more then others. Chemcials such as olefins can sell for alot, and are abundant in plastic, primaily HDPE plastic.
The process of turning HDPE into these chemcials is a long process, but in short you heat the plastic by pyolysis, then hydroformylation. This creates the valuable olefins, then hydrogenate the olefins.
Once the full process is done you are left with high value chemicals, that can the be resold back into the market to make plastic, but also other oil/petrolium based products.

**Why it matters to our project:**  
This allows us to turn metaphorically, plastic into liquid gold. These chemcials often sell near the value it takes to make them. 
This creates a large oppetunity to make large sums of money sellng these machines.

**Source:**  
Hydroformylation of pyrolysis oils to aldehydes and alcohols from polyolefin waste:  https://www.science.org/doi/full/10.1126/science.adh1853?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery

